Package: hchg
Type: Package
Title: Higher Criticism Tests for Non-Proportional Hazard Deviations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alon", "Kipnis", email = "alon.kipnis@runi.ac.il",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ben", "Galili", role = "aut"),
    person("Zohar", "Yakhini", role = "aut"))
Description: Omnibus tests for comparing two right-censored survival samples
    that are powerful against sparse departures from equal hazards, where the
    hazard difference is concentrated in a small and a priori unknown subset of
    the follow-up. Exact hypergeometric p-values are computed for each time
    interval and aggregated with the Higher Criticism statistic of Donoho and
    Jin (2004) <doi:10.1214/009053604000000265>, or alternatively with the
    Berk-Jones, Fisher or minimum-p statistics. Global p-values are obtained by
    permuting group labels, and the intervals driving a detection can be
    recovered for diagnostic plotting. The method is described in Kipnis,
    Galili and Yakhini (2026) <doi:10.1093/biomet/asaf075>.
